; Does the southbridge report RELEASED for ordinary keys, or only for modifiers?
;
;   load "keystate
;   keystate
;
; RUN AND PASSED on a Pico Plus 2 W, 2026-08-14: DOWN followed the finger and
; released cleanly, and HIT appeared once per press rather than once per
; firmware repeat.  That settles the question this file was written to ask, and
; the three games depend on the answer -- so it stays here as the regression
; check for any future change to the driver, not as an open investigation.
;
; The key-state mechanism -- `pollkeys`, `keydown?`, `keyhit?` -- is built on
; the answer being "all keys".  devices/picocalc/keyboard.c sets a key's bit on
; KEY_STATE_PRESSED and clears it on KEY_STATE_RELEASED, so if the firmware
; sends a release only for shift/ctrl/alt (which is all the driver handled
; before this change, and therefore all the source proves), every ordinary key
; would latch down on its first press and never come up.  That cannot be tested
; on the host: `tests/test_keyboard.c` drives a FIFO this file's author wrote,
; so it can only confirm the driver believes what it was told.
;
; This runs the real bus.  Hold each key in turn: DOWN must follow your finger,
; not stick.  If a key shows DOWN after you have let go, releases are not being
; reported for it and the mechanism needs a timeout fallback.
;
; HIT is the other half: it must show for exactly one line per press, however
; long you hold the key -- the firmware repeats a held key ten times a second
; and those repeats must not read as fresh presses.
;
; Press Q to finish.

to keystate
  cleartext
  pr [Hold each key.  DOWN must follow your finger.]
  pr [HIT must appear once per press, not per repeat.]
  pr [Q to quit.]
  pr []
  pollkeys                   ; baseline: drop whatever started this
  until [keydown? 113] [keystate.frame]
  pr []
  pr [Done.]
end

; One line per frame, at roughly a game's frame rate, so the display shows the
; same view of the keyboard a game would get.
to keystate.frame
  pollkeys
  keystate.show "|left | 180
  keystate.show "|right| 183
  keystate.show "|up   | 181
  keystate.show "|space| 32
  wait 4
end

to keystate.show :name :code
  if not (or (keydown? :code) (keyhit? :code)) [stop]
  type :name
  type "| |
  if keydown? :code [type "|DOWN |]
  if keyhit? :code [type "HIT]
  pr []
end
